WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.868
-Ana Gasteyer, Rachel Dratch!
-Yes!

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:04.067
-Hi!
-Hello. Jimmy.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:06.000
-You guys look fantastic.
It's great to see you.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.234
I missed you.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:10.200
-We missed you too.
-We missed you too, Jimmy!

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.767
-"Jimmy, we miss you, Jimmy!"

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.501
Can you believe we've
known each other 20 years?

00:00:16.501 --> 00:00:17.501
-Oh, my God.
-So long.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:18.801
-Does that make any sense?

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.734
-Yeah, well, more than that,
because Frances is 19,

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:23.868
and she was born
when I left "Saturday Night."

00:00:23.868 --> 00:00:25.734
So we've known each other for --
-Over 20 years.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:27.601
-Maybe 24.
-Oh, my Lord.

00:00:27.601 --> 00:00:28.968
-How are the kids?
-Everybody's good.

00:00:28.968 --> 00:00:30.067
-They're great.
Everyone's great.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.300
-Yeah.
-Do they watch you?

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:33.300
I mean, they're at the age
they know your work now.

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:35.434
-So, Frances is over it,
because she's in college.

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:36.701
She's just
officially embarrassed.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:38.067
-She's in college?
-Yeah, she's in college.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:42.267
My 13-year-old loves
"Schweddy Balls," obviously.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.701
-As we all do. Yeah, of course.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.367
-Well, not because of that.
-It's an American classic.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:48.000
-Not because of that,
but because of the content.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.467
But then, so, we were watching
a Christmas show the other day,

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.868
because it came on.

00:00:50.868 --> 00:00:52.767
You know, the Christmas special
they do on "SNL" thing.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.367
And I was actually --
We were in a hotel.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:55.601
We were down for Thanksgiving.

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.367
And "Topless Christmas" came on,

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.467
and that was
"Martha Stewart's Topless..."

00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:00.267
-"Martha Stewart's
Topless Christmas."

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:01.501
-"Martha Stewart's
Topless Christmas."

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:02.834
-And you played Martha Stewart.

00:01:02.834 --> 00:01:04.234
-Yeah, and that was
actually the first time

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.267
that he was ashamed.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.267
He turned, like,
the most amazing color of red,

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.300
and he doesn't
blush easily, so....

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:14.467
-That was such a good bit.
Ana, you have a new show on NBC.

00:01:14.467 --> 00:01:16.968
-I do.
-Debuting on Monday.

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:18.901
-Is it on Monday?
-December 13th.

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:20.267
-Monday...
-Yeah. Monday-ish.

00:01:20.267 --> 00:01:22.534
-...December 13th, yeah.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.767
-What a long pause.
It's on Monday. Is it?

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:27.734
-It's Monday after this Monday.
-Yeah, not this Monday.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:28.834
-Yeah.
-Monday, December 13th.

00:01:28.834 --> 00:01:30.434
-December 13th.
-Yeah, that's correct.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:31.868
That's when it comes out.
-It's after "The Voice."

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:33.501
-"American Auto."
-Blake Shelton's "The Voice."

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:34.634
-It's after "The Voice."
-Yeah.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:36.000
-That's a good lead-in.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.000
-They're doing a sneak peek
of the first two episodes,

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.901
and then it starts airing
for real in January.

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:41.067
And it's set --

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:44.501
It's Justin Spitzer,
who created "Superstore."

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.701
It's his new show.
It's an office comedy.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:48.067
NBC, you know -- they love a

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:51.501
half-hour office-oriented
comedy, workplace comedy.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:54.000
And it's set in
the automotive industry,

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.067
and I play the new female C.E.O.

00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:58.601
I come from Big Pharma.
I've got questionable morals.

00:01:58.601 --> 00:02:02.701
And I don't know
anything about cars.

00:02:02.701 --> 00:02:04.767
-Perfect place to work then.
Yeah, why not?

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.634
-So, that's it.
That's in a nutshell.

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:07.701
It's really fun.
It's a great show.

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:09.033
I'm excited about it.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:10.701
-And then let's talk
about "Clusterfunke Christmas."

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:12.033
-Yeah.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:14.601
-By the way, already,
I was laughing at the trailer.

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.701
And then I go, "Oh, my God.
I got to watch this."

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:19.167
I love Hallmark movies.
I love Lifetime movies.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.834
I'm honest. I love them.

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:21.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
I absolutely love them. Right?

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:22.968
-They're the best.

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.167
-I think they --
I don't know what it is.

00:02:24.167 --> 00:02:25.467
I just love it.

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:28.300
I go, "Oh, my gosh,
why has no one spoofed this?"

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.067
And you crushed it.
-And that's what we've done.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.267
-Now, where did you -- Yeah.
-So, Jimmy, let me tell you.

00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:34.801
This is a parody of a

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.067
Hallmark/Lifetime
Christmas movie.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.734
And we just wanted to do --
You know, like you said,

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.567
we thought this was an area
that's ripe for parody.

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:42.667
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.000
We enjoy an
"Airplane!"-style spoof.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:47.067
-Yeah, sort of our model
was the movie "Airplane!",

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.400
if you applied that to --

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.567
-And we couldn't believe
no one had done it.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.267
And, like you,
we've watched thousands of them,

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.367
and they all pretty much
have the same plot.

00:02:53.367 --> 00:02:54.767
So it seemed pretty easy to,
you know --

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.267
-Right. So we picked the plot
that we've seen the most,

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:58.567
which is like,
you know, big-time --

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:01.667
like, executive woman
in the big city

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.901
who has no time
for love or Christmas

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:07.067
gets sent by her business
to a small town,

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.300
where she meets a, like, insert
small-town profession here.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.734
-Craftsperson, a craftsman.

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:11.901
-Lumberjack, toy-maker,
what have you.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:13.067
-Yeah, sleigh-maker.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:14.801
-And then, at first --
And she's just there

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:16.267
to take over a quaint business.

00:03:16.267 --> 00:03:18.133
And, at first,
they don't get along.

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:19.734
They butt heads.
But then, guess what.

00:03:19.734 --> 00:03:21.033
I wonder if she's going to find

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.334
love and
the spirit of Christmas.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.334
-She might find
the spirit of Christmas.

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:24.567
-We don't want to
ruin the ending.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:26.033
-We don't want to ruin it,
but it does happen.

00:03:26.033 --> 00:03:27.868
-It does.
-Yeah.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.200
-That's the best way
anyone's ever summed up

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.934
any project that they've come on
the show to talk about.

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:34.400
-There's also a stray dog.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.901
We threw in everything
that you've ever seen.

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:37.167
-Every trope we could think of
we tried to throw in.

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.467
-Meaningful snowfall.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.200
It starts snowing when there's
a big, emotional moment.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.467
-Lot of cocoa.
-Lots of hot chocolate.

00:03:42.467 --> 00:03:44.067
-A questionably gay
platonic friend.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:45.434
-Yeah.

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.501
-We threw in whatever
we could throw in there.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.133
-It's all in there.
It's all there.

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:49.767
-And we, naturally,
play the spinsters,

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:51.300
the old spinsters
who run the inn.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.167
-So, when we were talking about
what we might do in this movie,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.033
there was just --
there wasn't even a discussion.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.868
Like, one of us just said like,
"And we're going to play

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.167
the old spinsters
that run the inn, right?"

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:00.601
It was like, "Yeah, of course."

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.601
Because it's like we wanted to
put on the gray buns --

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:07.033
-We got our Party City buns.
-Yeah, Party City hairdos.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:08.367
-Because the thing is,
in these worlds,

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:10.133
in the Hallmark and Lifetime
world, as you know,

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:13.467
you're either an ingenue
and you're eligible for breeding

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.934
or you're Mrs. Claus.

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.801
There is really no...

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.501
-You know what I like,
is the songs,

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:21.100
the actual holiday songs,
the Christmas songs in this.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.767
-Well, so, you're -- If you are
a student of these films,

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:27.000
they're all made for $15
in Vancouver in July, okay?

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.534
-That's where we shot it.
-And that's where we shot it.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.634
That's where we shot it.

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:30.834
And there's Christmas
in every frame.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:32.334
And it's like a machine
that just, like,

00:04:32.334 --> 00:04:33.667
churns out these
amazing holiday parodies.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:35.734
-And there's product placement.
-Product placement.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.067
We have that throughout.
Lots of product placement.

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:39.667
-But you can't do real --
Like, there's a lot of movies

00:04:39.667 --> 00:04:41.033
that they want to start with
"Jingle Bell Rock,"

00:04:41.033 --> 00:04:42.367
but they can't
afford the rights,

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.868
so there's -- It sort of sounds
like "Jingle Bell Rock."

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:48.367
So we wrote some songs
like that, "Jangle Ball Shake."

00:04:48.367 --> 00:04:50.033
-Yeah, "Jangle Bell Shake."

00:04:50.033 --> 00:04:52.634
-And instead of "All I Want
for Christmas is You"...

00:04:52.634 --> 00:04:53.767
-By Mariah Carey.

00:04:53.767 --> 00:04:56.234
-...it's "All I Have for
Christmas is Fruit"

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:57.734
by Shaniah Gary.

00:04:57.734 --> 00:04:59.300
-Ooh!
-It's close.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.567
People overeat
around that time of the year,

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:01.667
so it has a nice message.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:02.834
-It's just in
the background, though.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.400
That's not a theme in the movie.
-Yes, it's great.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.067
Anyways, I want to show
everyone a clip here.

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:08.334
This is Ana Gasteyer
and Rachel Dratch in

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:10.067
"A Clusterfunke Christmas."

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:11.634
Take a look at this.

00:05:11.634 --> 00:05:12.934
-What I'm trying to say is,

00:05:12.934 --> 00:05:15.567
I'm not just here
for the upcoming Bonfire Fest,

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:16.734
as lovely as it seems.

00:05:16.734 --> 00:05:18.100
-Let me guess.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.133
You came to get away from
the breakneck pace of your life

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:21.167
as an executive in the city.

00:05:21.167 --> 00:05:22.968
-No. I am --

00:05:22.968 --> 00:05:24.200
-Got fired?
-No.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.567
-Widowed?
-No.

00:05:25.567 --> 00:05:26.701
-Runaway bride?
-No.

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:27.801
-You inherited a bookstore
here in town?

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:28.968
-No.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.634
-You're a single mom
whose husband ditched out

00:05:30.634 --> 00:05:32.334
on the family, and now
you're here to meet up with

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.868
a single dad whose wife
ditched out on his family

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:36.734
so you can blend both families
together by Christmas?

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:39.067
-You came to run a
Christmas children's chorus

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:40.567
and find your own voice
in the process?

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:43.133
-You have amnesia,
wandered into town by accident,

00:05:43.133 --> 00:05:45.334
and won't remember your identity
until Christmas morning?

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:46.901
-Your boyfriend is
here for the winter,

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:49.834
but he's secretly a prince of
a small Slavic nation.

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:52.801
-You're here to track down
the owner of a locket you found

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.300
hidden away
in a Christmas ornament.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.734
-That's locked inside
a music box.

00:05:55.734 --> 00:05:58.167
-That's been hidden away
in your attic for 40 years?

00:05:58.167 --> 00:05:59.167
-No.

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:01.834
-Oh.
-Oh.

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:03.734
-That is how you do it.

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:05.801
That is exactly
how you do it right there.

00:06:05.801 --> 00:06:07.300
Ana Gasteyer, Rachel Dratch.

